✔ (c) the bench captions: "upper fence at 19" and "IQR 4.5" against the drawn numbers are ONE message that names both and gives the full drawn set (16.6274ms)
✔ (c) first / lower quartile read as Q1 and third / upper quartile as Q3 (2.6365ms)
✔ (c) the message is truncate-safe: every wrong statement, then the full drawn set once, whole inside the repair problem even with other numbers problems after it (4.3467ms)
✔ (c) operands, a following word and equations are not read as the statistic; the typography of the saved bench cards neither (13.8992ms)
✔ (c) half a unit of the decimals written; with two boxes a number may name any box; a card with no box plot is not read; IQR is a derived path a token can name (16.4703ms)
✔ (c) the one message of a one-box card fits the 480-character cut that applies to the other messages (measured) (0.8577ms)
✔ the route: no values and wrong typed statistics come out with the learner's values and the computed statistics; the trace says what was set and changed (798.0902ms)
✔ the route: two lists in the question fill nothing and reject nothing; the trace counts them (61.4511ms)
✔ (c) a unit after the number is part of the statistic: "IQR is 14.5 ms" and "upper fence at 122.75 ms" are read (the v2 bench captions); copulas and prepositions between term and number (3.2455ms)
✔ (c) v4-1: the result of "<term> is a - b = c" is compared with the drawn statistic; the operands stay skipped (the v3 idx 15 caption) (2.8511ms)
✔ (c) v4-2: "lands at", "comes to", "works out to" (and "sits at") connect a term to its number (the v3 idx 15 prose) (2.2034ms)
✔ (c) v4-3: number words are read as numbers before the scan (hyphenated, spaced, "point" decimals); a lone "one" and hundreds are left alone (3.2381ms)
